WHY THIS FILE EXISTS RATHER THAN AN OPEN-SOURCE LICENCE

Until 2026-08-22 this repository had no LICENCE file and no `license` field, which left its
status undefined. "All rights reserved" is the legal default in that situation, so this file
changes nothing substantive — it states the position instead of leaving it to be inferred.

That is deliberately the conservative direction. An open-source licence GRANTS rights, and a
grant is far harder to withdraw than to make. This repository's eventual ownership is not
settled, and material has been ported into it from RootCawsLLC/proofplane, which is licensed
AGPL-3.0-or-later to third parties. RootCawsLLC holds the copyright in both, so relicensing its
own work is its own to do — but doing so should be a decision somebody makes, not a side effect
of a default.

Relicensing later is one file. Un-granting is not.
